 12, "output_tokens": 0}, "msg_047832f350e69220016ac1b979eaf087d0b2df191b315384cf": {"cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0, "content": [{"cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 33, "output_tokens": 0}], "input_tokens": 33, "output_tokens": 0}, "fc_047832f350e69220016ac1b97aeb9087d0913e6c49315c0fe1": {"cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 24, "output_tokens": 0}, "fco_01a104bc-b3b8-73f2-b6f3-3ca6d61e6987": {"cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0, "content": [{"cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 22, "output_tokens": 0}], "input_tokens": 22, "output_tokens": 0}, "amsg_01a104bc-b3ba-7772-affa-725bd10e4557": {"cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 439, "output_tokens": 0}, "fc_047832f350e69220016ac1b987138487d08a7e15c5aa629644": {"cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 0, "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 22}}}, "input_tokens": 21696, "input_tokens_details": {"cache_write_tokens": 0, "cached_tokens": 20992}, "output_tokens": 22, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0}, "total_tokens": 21718}, "user": null, "metadata": {}}, "sequence_number": 13, "safety_buffering": false}
2026-10-04T02:27:24.236505Z TRACE tungstenite::protocol: Received message {"type": "response.output_item.done", "item": {"id": "ctc_00392a9ea231d83c016ac1b9802e3487d0b7efefa6c77eb27e", "type": "custom_tool_call", "status": "completed", "call_id": "call_GxkPxaYdZKxfbPDcWvkbo24Q", "input": "const draft = `At dawn, the river looks almost still, holding a pale copy of the sky between its banks. A heron waits beside the reeds, patient as driftwood, while minnows disturb the surface with rings no wider than coins. Upstream, rain from distant hills has already begun its slow descent toward this bend.\n\nBy noon, the water has changed character. Sunlight breaks across its current in hard, white flashes. Cottonwood leaves turn their silver undersides to the wind. Children test the cold shallows with bare feet, then retreat laughing when the mud releases bubbles around their toes. Beneath the bridge, shadows gather around old stones.\n\nThe river carries more than water. It moves pollen, branches, seeds, feathers, soil, and the faint mineral taste of places beyond sight. It remembers factories through rusted bolts and farms through traces of fertilizer. Near town, it accepts storm drains without ceremony, bearing every careless choice toward someone living farther downstream.\n\nAfter sunset, voices fade from the bank. Bats stitch quick paths above the current, hunting insects that rise from the cooling surface. A beaver crosses under the moon, leaving a narrow wake that opens, softens, and disappears. The river keeps moving through darkness, guided by gravity and the shape of the land.\n\nBy morning, none of its water will occupy quite the same place. The bend will look familiar, but the river will be newly assembled from rain, springs, runoff, and tributaries. That is its quiet bargain with every settlement along its course: it arrives as a gift, receives whatever people give back, and passes the account onward. To stand beside it is to watch time become visible, flowing past one rooted body toward an unseen sea.`;\nconst r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"python3 -c 'import sys; s=sys.stdin.read(); print(len(s.split()))'\",\"workdir\":\"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-richard-src-GitHub-rjmurillo-ai-agents/b0ef9425-9658-47ce-8d58-44b956717241/scratchpad/cx160/work/h\",\"yield_time_ms\":10000,\"max_output_tokens\":1000});\nconst w = await tools.write_stdin({session_id:r.session_id??0, chars:draft, yield_time_ms:1000, max_output_tokens:1000});\ntext(JSON.stringify({initial:r.output, final:w.output}));\n", "internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough": {"create_time": 1791080828.178194, "turn_id": "01a104bc-63a1-70a0-8485-f1d3e70e9511"}, "name": "exec", "metadata": {"turn_id": "01a104bc-63a1-70a0-8485-f1d3e70e9511"}}, "output_index": 1, "sequence_number": 504}
